{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1380690-the-nature-of-bonus-successes","id":1380690,"title":"The Nature of Bonus Successes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-12T10:16:45-07:00","id":1380690,"title":"The Nature of Bonus Successes","content":"This is a question, that I'll give two examples for, but both link back to my Garou, a Get of Fenris Fostern, about to make Adren, Ahroun, who is a terminator in the battlefield, but a cuddly gay puppy, when he isn't ripping jawbones out.<br /> <br /> The first example, was when another tribemate, of lower rank, but older than him, was undergoing the Rite of War. He attempted to block, a claw swipe, and got 8 Successes, unfortunately for him, my Get is also a badass, and like I said, a bit of nightmare on the field, and got 12 Successes, 4 Over the block. What would that look like skill-wise, or how would you RP that or describe it as the ST?<br /> <br /> The second example, is when he did something else. He is.....obscenely skilled in multiple areas. His Gnosis and Rage aren't what you'd expect of someone about to make Adren, nor that many gifts, but his WP is 8, and he has at least 6, if not higher as his dicepool for a number of skills. So much so, that when he went to pickpocket someone, take their wallet, put $200 in it, as an act of kindness, and put it back, he got 9 Successes, whereas they got 4 on the awareness check, meaning he got 5 over on his act of Larceny. How would you describe that, or play it as an ST? The total successes got knocked down to 4 or 5, but in both cases beforehand, it was at 9 or above.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12039-punkmaniak","name":"PunkManiak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12039_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T12:19:33-07:00","id":1380734,"title":"","content":"Better timing, less awkward motion, being in a temporary blind spot, picking up on a subtle weakness in an opponent's action... there's not really a set and absolute list of anything that might come up when comparing opposed tests. Sufficiently high successes might change the scale of operation, but between the parties involved, more successes means that they got one over the other. If it was a lot over the other, the opposing party might be at a complete loss to realize how or why without some serious self-analysis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T13:47:25-07:00","id":1380758,"title":"","content":"First, I use the net successes because it's just plain easier to describe a 4 success attack than a 12 success attack with the guidance from the books. I base a lot of flair (such as skill vs. luck) around that based on the character traits rather than the successes rolled. A master martial artist with Dexterity 5 and Brawl 5 that nets 5 successes and a street brawler with Dexterity 3 and Brawl 2 that nets 5 successes are going to get narrated more to highlight their base stats translating into that awesome hit.<br /> <br /> Beyond that... well... over 5 successes just doesn't matter to me in terms of trying to describe it. For better or worse the game puts this on a 0-5 scale descriptively, with 5 successes being a complete and total success. It's not worth the mental energy of trying to constantly squeeze out more to make a 6 success attack better than 5, and 7 better than 6, etc.<br /> <br /> Again, focus on the traits that help generate the successes, those are more interesting and varied than the net successes are going to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-12T14:21:26-07:00","id":1380768,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> To be fair. In this case, the character is a Master Martial Artist, as is his tribemate and compatriot. Difference is, where my PC Jack is in a pack under Mammoth and therefore has 7 Strength, Erik the other is packed under Firedrake and has 7 in Brawl as a result. They're of similar skill and strength without their totems, but Jack just hits like a damned tank. Literally a nightmare on the battlefield, with perfect physical stats.<br /> <br /> As for his Pickpocketing skill, he's more just insanely fast, than he is skilled. So I figure it could have been that he just moved to fast, and acted to fast for the other to catch on too what was going on, or catch him doing it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12039-punkmaniak","name":"PunkManiak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12039_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"275"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}